\title{cliqueR: Lineage tracing analysis with the clique toolkit}
\description{
\code{cliqueR} connects the \code{clique} Rust command-line application to R. The CLI
aligns amplicon reads, extracts and corrects capture tags, collapses
molecule groups, and annotates CRISPR events. The R package provides
configuration and execution helpers plus BAM import, character-matrix,
tree-reconstruction, and visualization tools.

The Rust binary is installed separately. Use \code{\link[=clique_binary]{clique_binary()}} to inspect
the executable selected for the current session or \code{\link[=set_clique_binary]{set_clique_binary()}} to
override it.
}
\section{Running clique}{

\code{\link[=fasta_targets_to_yaml]{fasta_targets_to_yaml()}} creates a basic read-structure YAML from reference
and target sequences. \code{\link[=generate_clique_script]{generate_clique_script()}} writes a reproducible
align/sort/collapse shell script. \code{\link[=clique_run]{clique_run()}} is the lower-level interface
for CLI subcommands and flags not represented by the script generator.

The typed \code{\link[=align]{align()}} and \code{\link[=collapse]{collapse()}} functions are reserved APIs and are not
implemented in this development release.
}

\section{Reading and analyzing results}{

\code{\link[=read_longread_lineage]{read_longread_lineage()}} imports selected auxiliary tags from an aligned or
collapsed BAM. \code{\link[=build_indel_matrix]{build_indel_matrix()}} turns the \code{ce} edit tag into integer
character states, \code{\link[=indel_distance]{indel_distance()}} computes pairwise distances while
ignoring missing calls, and the \verb{tree_*()} functions reconstruct lineage
trees. \code{\link[=tree_nj]{tree_nj()}} and \code{\link[=tree_parsimony]{tree_parsimony()}} run in R; \code{\link[=tree_iqtree]{tree_iqtree()}},
\code{\link[=tree_vine]{tree_vine()}}, \code{\link[=tree_mix]{tree_mix()}}, and \code{\link[=tree_cassiopeia]{tree_cassiopeia()}} connect optional
external backends. Use \code{\link[=plot_lineage_tree]{plot_lineage_tree()}} to add categorical or
continuous tip annotations.
}

\section{BAM tags}{

Capture tags are named \code{e0} through \code{e9} from their YAML symbols; collapsed
BAMs can also contain original values \code{o0} through \code{o9}. \code{ce} stores
chemistry-filtered event calls, \code{pe} stores prime-edit classifications, \code{rc}
is corrected-group depth, \code{dc} is consensus depth after downsampling, and
\code{ar} lists the selected source-read names. See
\code{vignette("bam-output", package = "cliqueR")} for the complete contract.
}

\section{Optional dependencies}{

Most analysis and visualization dependencies are in \code{Suggests} and are
checked only by the functions that need them. \code{samtools} must be available
to \code{\link[=read_longread_lineage]{read_longread_lineage()}}. The \code{clique} Rust executable is a separate
system requirement. IQ-TREE 2, VINE, PHYLIP MIX, and the Python Cassiopeia
package are optional and only needed by their corresponding tree functions.
}

